# Pi workflow reference

Env-specific facts, dated; if behavior seems changed, verify against the source repo and
update this file. Sandbox, modes, approvals: `sandbox.md`; measurements: the audit log.

## Launch and pins (last verified 2026-09-26)

- The managed `pi` zsh function runs the lockfile-pinned CLI (currently {{ index (fromJson (include "package.json")).dependencies "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent" }}, one
  pin with the extensions and worker SDK) with native tools and ambient extensions
  off; a binary run outside it bypasses the workflow. Sessions load the applied
  `~/.pi/agent`, so a source edit needs `chezmoi apply`. Sign in through Pi's
  OpenAI subscription login; do not import another harness's auth files.

## Models (last verified 2026-09-25)

- Default: `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.provider }}/{{ index .subagent_tiers.pi .agents.pi.defaults.tier }}`, {{ .agents.pi.defaults.reasoning_effort }} reasoning.
- The approval classifier (MCP calls, remote-mutating shell verbs, unsandboxed requests)
  runs two tool-less stages: `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_filter.model }}` at {{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_filter.reasoning_effort }} reasoning screens each reviewed action; anything
  but allow goes to `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_judge.model }}` at {{ .agents.pi.defaults.classifier_judge.reasoning_effort }} reasoning on the same prompt, whose verdict is final.
- Specialist roles, from `subagents` in agents.yaml (which records each why):

| role | model | reasoning |
|---|---|---|
{{ range $name, $role := includeTemplate "pi-roles" (dict "root" .) | fromJson -}}
| {{ $name }} | `{{ $role.model }}` | {{ $role.thinking }} |
{{ end }}
- `workflow/children.mjs` rejects frontier children. The `{{ .subagent_tiers.pi.frontier }}` pin is in
  the SDK's subscription catalog; if dropped, fail unavailable, not an alias or API billing.
- All models draw one plan allowance at their own rate ([live rate card](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/pricing));
  API task cost is not Pro allowance; compare completed tasks including retries.
- Context window: 272,000 input tokens on the subscription route (pinned catalog,
  2026-09-26); the model pages' 1,050,000 is API-key only. It has moved without
  notice: trust the live readout (status line, `/session`; pi has no `/status`).

## Specialists and skills (last verified 2026-09-22)

- Specialists under `~/.pi/agent/agents` render from the shared roster with an
  explicit model, tool list and policy extension; read-only ones stay read-only in
  execution. Only `general-purpose` may launch children, to Claude Code's depth.
- Children run in the background, up to twenty sharing the root policy (Claude Code's default),
  start fresh with no channel back (intercom off, 2026-09-10); batch independent launches.
- Scripts/chains, role overrides, revival and mutating management are refused; status, stop,
  interrupt and steer work. Runs stop at two hours, with a checkpoint steer five minutes before.
- Skills load only by explicit `/skill:name` (2026-09-26). A child's allowlist may
  leave direct `mcp__*` tools inactive; the always-allowed `mcp` proxy reaches them.

## Web search (last verified 2026-09-23)

- `web_search` is the pinned `pi-web-search` plugin: OpenAI's server-side search
  on the ChatGPT-subscription endpoint model calls use — no extra credential or
  network path, and the provider's own terms grey zone. Each search is one extra
  request on the usage windows, at the small tier set in `~/.pi/agent/web-search.json`.
  Roles with Claude's `WebSearch` get it (Gemini-only `url_context` in none); fetch
  with Exa or Playwright.

## MCP and code intelligence (last verified 2026-09-22)

- Context7 tools stay direct (e.g. `mcp__context7_query-docs`); Exa and Playwright
  stay behind the `mcp` proxy: `mcp({ search: "…" })` finds a tool in the cached
  catalog, `mcp({ describe: "<name>" })` shows its schema, `mcp({ tool: "<name>",
  args: { … } })` calls it; a server shown as not connected connects on first call.
- MCP servers other than Playwright (see `sandbox.md`) run inside SRT; Node servers
  use `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` so fetch follows the sandbox proxy. If every call
  fails with `fetch failed`, check that setting, then the allowed domains.
- Config is explicit, not imported from other harnesses. MCP scripting, namespace
  proxies, semantic search, sampling and OAuth discovery are off; tools a server
  adds after startup are reachable only via `mcp`. Approval checks the resolved call.
- No LSP: diagnostics come from project toolchains via `workspace_bash` (`tsc --noEmit`,
  `go vet`, pyright, linters). Claude's proprietary plugins and cloud services: use Claude.
